; TEST: emit-exit=5
;
; `iconst u8 256`: not a value of u8, so not a u8 in canonical form
; (ssa-ir.md 2.2) -- verifier rule 1 (verify.inc's `__bfa_verify_pa_iconst`).
; A constant is where a value enters the function, so it is where the
; canonical form is checked; every other instruction assumes it. The emitter
; refuses the same text by name (exit 4), because `exsc` reaches the emitter
; without the verifier -- this fixture's 5 says the verifier got there
; first.
;
; Mutation (run): the verifier's check dropped -> emit_ir exits 4 (the
; emitter's refusal), not 5.

functio @initium (ptr) -> u8 {
b0:
%0 = param ptr 0
%1 = iconst u8 256
ret %1
}
